cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gpu-offload in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "gpu-offload: transparent CPU-to-GPU offloading of BLAS and LAPACK calls for unmodified programs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Alshizawi"
    given-names: "Jaifar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jaifar530/cpu-to-gpu-offloading"
url: "https://jaifar530.github.io/cpu-to-gpu-offloading/"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-10-05"
abstract: >-
  gpu-offload is an LD_PRELOAD library and command-line tool for Linux that runs the BLAS and
  LAPACK calls of unmodified programs on an NVIDIA GPU when a per-machine calibration predicts a
  speedup, with automatic CPU fallback. A cost model fitted from measurements of each operation,
  precision and problem size on the machine's own CPU and GPU decides per call, including the cost
  of data copies, and is corrected at run time.
keywords:
  - GPU offloading
  - transparent acceleration
  - BLAS
  - LAPACK
  - CUDA
  - cuBLAS
  - cuSOLVER
  - LD_PRELOAD
  - heterogeneous computing
  - auto-tuning
  - NumPy
